  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 14-layer alternating ZnS/ZnSe multilayer stack on Ge substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: ZnS, ZnSe, ZnS, ZnSe, ZnS, ZnSe, ZnS, ZnSe, ZnS, ZnSe, ZnS, ZnSe, ZnS, ZnSe (14 finite layers). Use coherent TMM solver. Initialize all layer thicknesses at quarter-wave optical thickness for 9500 nm center wavelength (approximately 1080 nm for ZnS n≈2.2, 990 nm for ZnSe n≈2.4). Set thickness bounds 500-2000 nm for all layers. Optimize for maximum transmittance in 8000-11000 nm band and minimum transmittance in 3000-5000 nm band. Sample spectrum at 2001 points from 3000-11000 nm. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with learning rate 0.03. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 8000-11000 nm, 3000-5000 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 8000-11000 nm band; Low transmittance in 3000-5000 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: High transmittance in 3000-5000 nm band. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count not exceeding 16.",
